{
  "requirement": "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to describe sites exactly as the site queries select them, to state as an obligation any convention the queries rely on, such as how a list is named, and to state only per-site obligations that a reviewer can check from the site and the helpers it calls.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has three obligations on the bundled skills. They must direct agents to (1) describe sites exactly as the site queries select them, (2) state as an obligation any convention the queries rely on, and (3) state only per-site obligations a reviewer can check from the site and the helpers it calls.\n\nThe single test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_describe_sites_as_queries_select_them_with_checkable_obligations]`. It reads the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md` through `distributed_reference`. `section` extracts the `## Do` and `## Don't` bodies with whitespace collapsed. `assert_text` asserts that each phrase is present, so a missing phrase fails the test.\n\n- **Obligations 1 and 2.** The test asserts the `## Do` section contains \"Describe sites exactly as the site queries select them. When a query relies on a convention, such as how a variable is named, state the convention as an obligation\". That covers both the directive to describe sites exactly and the directive to state the convention as an obligation. The \"how a variable is named\" example is illustrative, because the requirement says \"such as\". The bundled text does contain this guidance (searched in `assets/skills/habeas/references/distributed-requirements.md`, `## Do`).\n- **Obligation 1, negative form.** The test asserts the `## Don't` section contains \"Don't describe sites more broadly than the queries select\".\n- **Obligation 3.** The test asserts the `## Don't` section contains \"Don't state a per-site obligation that a reviewer cannot check from the site and the helpers it calls\". That matches the checkability clause.\n\nThe requirement concerns the presence of guidance text. Phrase-presence assertions on the specific sections where that guidance lives are therefore the appropriate check. The bundled skills have one home for this topic, and the other skills only refer to it. The tests for `requirements.cli.skill_structure.refer` and `requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.bootstrap` cover that referral, so the guidance does not need testing in every skill.\n\nI found no untested obligation, no wrong expectation and no ambiguity, and there are no acknowledgments to account for.",
